## A brief introduction to xref
## mix xref trace FILE
## mix xref graph
  * `--exclude` - path to exclude. Can be repeated to exclude multiple
  * `--label` - only shows relationships with the given label. The labels
  * `--group` - provide comma-separated paths to consider as a group.
  * `--only-direct` - keeps only files with the direct relationship given
  * `--only-nodes` - only shows the node names (no edges). Generally useful
  * `--source` - displays all files that the given source file references
  * `--sink` - displays all files that reference the given file (directly
  * `--min-cycle-size` - controls the minimum cycle size on formats like
  * `--min-cycle-label` - controls the minimum number of dependencies with
  * `--format` - can be set to one of:
  * `--output` *(since v1.15.0)* - can be used to override the location of
## Shared options
  * `--fail-above` - generates a failure if the relevant metric is above
  * `--include-siblings` - includes dependencies that have `:in_umbrella`
  * `--no-compile` - does not compile even if files require compilation
  * `--no-deps-check` - does not check dependencies
  * `--no-archives-check` - does not check archives
